experiment: switchrate
  SHORT RUN — 150000 ticks against a minimum of 450000. derived: §55. §54 imposed wrong writes in TRIAL-LENGTH blocks and found
  AVERAGING, leaving SHORT RUNS as the one candidate for the derived
  index's 3.3-4.0 SE deficit. `ctx_hist` is accumulated per window and both
  consumers take only its ARGMAX, so the histogram's CONCENTRATION -- the
  only within-window stability measure the session already produces -- has
  been discarded every time since §49. This reads it before imposing
  anything. PRIMARY: runlen = sum(live)/(sum(switches)+windows) in ticks,
  pooled as a ratio of sums; `pure1` and `purity` are reported and bear on
  no verdict, because purity cannot separate a fast flicker from two long
  blocks (both read 0.5). Verdict three ways on the 95% CI against the
  PROTOCOL's own timescales: >= 450 (half the 900-tick window, so at most
  one switch) REFUTES short runs; <= 150 (kFeedbackPeriodTicks, where
  reward and slot decouple inside one window) and it SURVIVES; a
  straddling CI is NO VERDICT and gets said. CLAUSE 0 is liveness, because
  §53's T-A printed PASS twice on an EMPTY SET. Two arms are EXACT
  self-tests (pin_mode 1 and 3 pin once per window: 0 switches, runlen
  900.0) and three are CALIBRATIONS -- pin_mode 4 re-draws over two slots
  every f ticks, and a fair coin leaves the slot alone half the time, so
  the estimator must read 2f truncated by the window (19.78 / 94.74 /
  225.00) and NOT f. kRead: every branch prints
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  the question      §55. §54 imposed wrong writes in TRIAL-LENGTH blocks (the pin
                    is set once per window) and found AVERAGING. Short runs are
                    the one candidate left for the derived index's 3.3-4.0 SE
                    deficit, and its run length has NEVER been measured.
  the quantity      runlen = sum(live) / (sum(switches) + windows), in ticks. A
                    SWITCH is a live tick whose slot differs from the previous
                    LIVE tick's. Pooled as a ratio of sums, not a mean of
                    per-window ratios (`mean-of-ratios`).
  the boundaries    A: CI lower >= 450 (<=1 switch/window) -- short runs REFUTED.
                    B: CI upper <= 150 (the feedback period) -- SURVIVES.
                    C: anything else, including a straddling CI. The estimator's
                    ceiling is 900 ticks by construction.
  session           150.0 s of simulated life x 84 sessions, 6 arms
  *** BELOW THE REGISTERED MINIMUM (150000 < 450000). A smoke resolves the
      EXACT self-tests and the calibration, which are properties of the
      instrument and not of the budget. It does NOT resolve the verdict.
  instrument        switchrate   trial seed 0000000001357269   84 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

